# {{.Name}}

This project uses Modary's Admin Profile. The composition is explicit in
`internal/app/application.go`: PostgreSQL, {{if .HasOIDC}}OIDC{{else}}local development password identity{{end}}, RBAC,
session HTTP, and the consumer-owned `records` slice.{{if .HasTasks}} River-backed
task inspection is selected.{{end}}{{if .HasAudit}} Scope-bound SQL audit inspection is selected.{{end}}
Governed Actions and MCP are not selected.

Set development configuration:

```sh
export DATABASE_URL='postgres://user:password@127.0.0.1:5432/app?sslmode=disable'
{{if .HasOIDC}}export MODARY_OIDC_ISSUER_URL='https://identity.example.com'
export MODARY_OIDC_CLIENT_ID='replace-with-client-id'
export MODARY_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET='replace-with-client-secret' # optional for public clients
export MODARY_OIDC_REDIRECT_URL='https://admin.example.com/api/auth/oidc/callback'
export MODARY_OIDC_SUBJECT='replace-with-exact-provider-subject'
{{else}}export MODARY_ADMIN_USERNAME='admin'
export MODARY_ADMIN_PASSWORD='replace-with-at-least-12-characters'
{{end}}
{{if .HasTasks}}export MODARY_QUEUE_SCHEMA={{.QueueSchemaID}}
{{end}}
export MODARY_ALLOW_INSECURE_COOKIE='true' # local HTTP only
{{if .HasOIDC}}# For a local HTTP-only provider, also set MODARY_OIDC_ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP=true.
{{end}}
```

Run the backend:

```sh
go run -mod=mod ./cmd/{{.ID}} migrate
go run -mod=mod ./cmd/{{.ID}} serve
```

The first command is a migration-only process and exits before serving. Serving
does not apply migrations unless `MODARY_MIGRATE_ON_START=true` is selected
explicitly for a controlled local workflow.

It listens on `127.0.0.1:8080` by default. `MODARY_HTTP_ADDR` and
`MODARY_DATABASE_SCHEMA` select another address or application schema.
Generated schema defaults use project-derived role prefixes, keeping application,
queue, and test namespaces distinct and outside PostgreSQL's reserved schemas.
Overlong names retain a readable prefix and add a deterministic hash fragment so
they remain within their PostgreSQL and River limits.

The Go binary embeds the production Admin UI, so running it does not require
Node.js. The source in `web/` uses React 19, TypeScript, Vite, React Router, and
an explicit Module registry. `src/App.tsx` composes session and route providers;
`src/modules/active.ts` selects source modules. `src/modules/index.ts` resolves
them against backend contribution descriptors and current actor grants.
The generated interface uses Simplified Chinese (`zh-CN`) for application
chrome and accessibility labels while preserving technical identifiers and
operational source values.

To customize the UI source, use the pinned pnpm toolchain:

```sh
cd web
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm lint
pnpm typecheck
pnpm test
pnpm build
pnpm assets:check
pnpm audit:prod
```

The build updates `internal/web/dist`; `assets:check` requires a byte-identical
clean rebuild. Bootstrap HTML uses `Cache-Control: no-cache`, while
content-hashed assets use ETags and `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000,
immutable`. A deployment therefore selects a new asset URL whenever its bytes
change without giving up long-lived caching for unchanged assets.
`audit:prod` rejects known high- or critical-severity production dependency
advisories through the public npm advisory service.

Run tests:

```sh
go mod tidy
go test ./...
```
